(1191, 'App\\Models\\User', 2, 'updated', 'App\\Models\\Blog', 10, '{\"short_content\":\"sd\",\"content\":\"<h2>Wazir-e-Azam Apna Ghar Programme: What You Actually Need to Know<\\/h2><p>Every month the rent goes out, and the same quiet question follows it: will we ever own a place of our own? For a lot of Pakistani families, the honest answer has been \\\"probably not.\\\" The <strong>Wazir-e-Azam Apna Ghar Programme<\\/strong>, also called <strong>\\\"Ghar Ho Tu Apna,\\\"<\\/strong> is the government\'s attempt to change that.<\\/p><h2>The Programme, Explained Simply<\\/h2><p>Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif launched it on 30 April 2026. The plan is to finance 500,000 homes over five years at a cost of Rs3.2 trillion. In year one, the target is 50,000 houses, with Rs321 billion set aside.<\\/p><p>It isn\'t a giveaway. It\'s a subsidised loan. You borrow from a participating bank, and the government covers part of the markup in the early years.<\\/p><h2>The Numbers, in Simple Terms<\\/h2><table><tr><th>Feature<\\/th><th>Details<\\/th><\\/tr><tr><td>Loan Size<\\/td><td>Up to Rs. 10 million<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Markup Rate<\\/td><td>5% fixed for the first 10 years<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Loan Tenure<\\/td><td>Up to 20 years<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Down Payment<\\/td><td>10% of the property value<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Bank Financing<\\/td><td>Up to 90% of the property value<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Processing Fees<\\/td><td>No processing charges<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Early Repayment<\\/td><td>No penalty for early repayment<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/table><p>After year ten, the rate moves to market level. It is around one-year KIBOR plus 3%, so your installment can climb. Plan for that now rather than being surprised later.<\\/p><p>During the subsidised period, estimated monthly installments are:<\\/p><listing><li>Rs25 Lakh loan works out to roughly Rs16,500 a month.<\\/li><li>Rs50 Lakh is about Rs33,000 a month.<\\/li><li>Rs75 Lakh is about Rs49,500 a month.<\\/li><li>Rs1 Crore is about Rs66,000 a month.<\\/li><\\/listing><p>These are estimates. Your bank will give you the exact figure.<\\/p><h2>What Can You Buy or Build?<\\/h2><p>You can buy a house or flat, buy a plot and build on it, or build on land you already own. There are size limits: a house up to 10 marla (2,720 sq. ft.) or a flat up to 1,500 sq. ft. It\'s for living in, so rental and investment properties don\'t count.<\\/p><h2>Who Qualifies?<\\/h2><p>The basic eligibility requirements are simple:<\\/p><ul><li>You need a valid CNIC.<\\/li><li>You must be a first-time homeowner.<\\/li><li>You can\'t have a housing unit in your name.<\\/li><li>You shouldn\'t have already used another housing scheme.<\\/li><li>Salaried people, business owners, freelancers and informal earners can all apply.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>The finer points vary a little from bank to bank:<\\/p><ul><li>Age between 25 and 60, with the loan maturing before 60 (salaried) or 65 (self-employed).<\\/li><li>Minimum income of Rs25,000 a month for you and Rs20,000 for a co-applicant.<\\/li><li>At least 2 years of employment if salaried, or 3 years of business proof if self-employed.<\\/li><li>Debt burden ratio under 33% of your net monthly income.<\\/li><li>A clean ECIB credit record.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Check your ECIB history before you apply. It\'s better to find a forgotten old dues problem yourself than to hear about it from the bank.<\\/p><h2>How to Apply<\\/h2><p>There are two routes:<\\/p><ul><li>You can go through the online portal at apnaghar.gov.pk.<\\/li><li>The process is also bank-driven, and you can simply visit any participating commercial bank, Islamic bank or microfinance bank. Either way, the bank makes the final call.<\\/li><\\/ul><h3>On the Portal<\\/h3><p>On the portal, the application process goes like this:<\\/p><listing><li>Create an account with your name, CNIC, mobile number, email and password.<\\/li><li>Log in and click Apply Now.<\\/li><li>Pick your income category: salaried, business, or informal.<\\/li><li>Choose your bank and branch.<\\/li><li>Select the purpose, enter the amount, and set your equity (you can put in more than 10%).<\\/li><li>Fill in personal details, plus co-applicant and guarantor information if needed.<\\/li><li>Add employment details, using your net income, not gross.<\\/li><li>Upload your documents, review everything, and submit.<\\/li><\\/listing><h3>Documents You Will Be Needing<\\/h3><p>Keep these documents ready:<\\/p><ul><li>CNIC (front and back).<\\/li><li>A recent photograph.<\\/li><li>Employment certificate and salary slip.<\\/li><li>Six months of bank statements.<\\/li><li>Account maintenance certificate (it\'s separate from the statement).<\\/li><li>Next of kin\'s CNIC.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Zameen also mentions utility bills and property papers if you already own a plot, and some banks may ask for 6 to 12 months of statements.<\\/p><h2>A Few Things Worth Knowing<\\/h2><ul><li>The bank\'s approved evaluator will value the property, so your own estimate won\'t count.<\\/li><li>Construction loans are released in phases tied to progress.<\\/li><li>Since there\'s no processing fee, anyone asking you for money to \\\"fast-track\\\" your file is a red flag. Pay nothing before approval.<\\/li><li>Freelancers and the self-employed should expect to show stronger paperwork, like bank statements and tax returns. Some people report the process can take a while, so start early.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"cover_image\":\"\\/images\\/saima_blog_cover.jpg\",\"faqs\":\"[]\"}', '{\"short_content\":\"Every month the rent goes out, and the same quiet question follows it: will we ever own a place of our own? For a lot of Pakistani families,\",\"content\":\"<h2>Wazir-e-Azam Apna Ghar Programme: What You Actually Need to Know<\\/h2><p>Every month the rent goes out, and the same quiet question follows it: will we ever own a place of our own? For a lot of Pakistani families, the honest answer has been \\\"probably not.\\\" The <strong>Wazir-e-Azam Apna Ghar Programme<\\/strong>, also called <strong>\\\"Ghar Ho Tu Apna,\\\"<\\/strong> is the government\'s attempt to change that.<\\/p><h2>The Programme, Explained Simply<\\/h2><p>Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif launched it on 30 April 2026. The plan is to finance 500,000 homes over five years at a cost of Rs3.2 trillion. In year one, the target is 50,000 houses, with Rs321 billion set aside.<\\/p><p>It isn\'t a giveaway. It\'s a subsidised loan. You borrow from a participating bank, and the government covers part of the markup in the early years.<\\/p><h2>The Numbers, in Simple Terms<\\/h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Feature<\\/th><th>Details<\\/th><\\/tr><tr><td>Loan Size<\\/td><td>Up to Rs. 10 million<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Markup Rate<\\/td><td>5% fixed for the first 10 years<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Loan Tenure<\\/td><td>Up to 20 years<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Down Payment<\\/td><td>10% of the property value<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Bank Financing<\\/td><td>Up to 90% of the property value<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Processing Fees<\\/td><td>No processing charges<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Early Repayment<\\/td><td>No penalty for early repayment<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><p>After year ten, the rate moves to market level. It is around one-year KIBOR plus 3%, so your installment can climb. Plan for that now rather than being surprised later.<\\/p><p>During the subsidised period, estimated monthly installments are:<\\/p><ul><li>Rs25 Lakh loan works out to roughly Rs16,500 a month.<\\/li><li>Rs50 Lakh is about Rs33,000 a month.<\\/li><li>Rs75 Lakh is about Rs49,500 a month.<\\/li><li>Rs1 Crore is about Rs66,000 a month.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>These are estimates. Your bank will give you the exact figure.<\\/p><h2>What Can You Buy or Build?<\\/h2><p>You can buy a house or flat, buy a plot and build on it, or build on land you already own. There are size limits: a house up to 10 marla (2,720 sq. ft.) or a flat up to 1,500 sq. ft. It\'s for living in, so rental and investment properties don\'t count.<\\/p><h2>Who Qualifies?<\\/h2><p>The basic eligibility requirements are simple:<\\/p><ul><li>You need a valid CNIC.<\\/li><li>You must be a first-time homeowner.<\\/li><li>You can\'t have a housing unit in your name.<\\/li><li>You shouldn\'t have already used another housing scheme.<\\/li><li>Salaried people, business owners, freelancers and informal earners can all apply.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>The finer points vary a little from bank to bank:<\\/p><ul><li>Age between 25 and 60, with the loan maturing before 60 (salaried) or 65 (self-employed).<\\/li><li>Minimum income of Rs25,000 a month for you and Rs20,000 for a co-applicant.<\\/li><li>At least 2 years of employment if salaried, or 3 years of business proof if self-employed.<\\/li><li>Debt burden ratio under 33% of your net monthly income.<\\/li><li>A clean ECIB credit record.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Check your ECIB history before you apply. It\'s better to find a forgotten old dues problem yourself than to hear about it from the bank.<\\/p><h2>How to Apply<\\/h2><p>There are two routes:<\\/p><ul><li>You can go through the online portal at apnaghar.gov.pk.<\\/li><li>The process is also bank-driven, and you can simply visit any participating commercial bank, Islamic bank or microfinance bank. Either way, the bank makes the final call.<\\/li><\\/ul><h3>On the Portal<\\/h3><p>On the portal, the application process goes like this:<\\/p><ul><li>Create an account with your name, CNIC, mobile number, email and password.<\\/li><li>Log in and click Apply Now.<\\/li><li>Pick your income category: salaried, business, or informal.<\\/li><li>Choose your bank and branch.<\\/li><li>Select the purpose, enter the amount, and set your equity (you can put in more than 10%).<\\/li><li>Fill in personal details, plus co-applicant and guarantor information if needed.<\\/li><li>Add employment details, using your net income, not gross.<\\/li><li>Upload your documents, review everything, and submit.<\\/li><\\/ul><h3>Documents You Will Be Needing<\\/h3><p>Keep these documents ready:<\\/p><ul><li>CNIC (front and back).<\\/li><li>A recent photograph.<\\/li><li>Employment certificate and salary slip.<\\/li><li>Six months of bank statements.<\\/li><li>Account maintenance certificate (it\'s separate from the statement).<\\/li><li>Next of kin\'s CNIC.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Zameen also mentions utility bills and property papers if you already own a plot, and some banks may ask for 6 to 12 months of statements.<\\/p><h2>A Few Things Worth Knowing<\\/h2><ul><li>The bank\'s approved evaluator will value the property, so your own estimate won\'t count.<\\/li><li>Construction loans are released in phases tied to progress.<\\/li><li>Since there\'s no processing fee, anyone asking you for money to \\\"fast-track\\\" your file is a red flag. Pay nothing before approval.<\\/li><li>Freelancers and the self-employed should expect to show stronger paperwork, like bank statements and tax returns. Some people report the process can take a while, so start early.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"cover_image\":\"\\/images\\/blogs\\/1794828956_cover_how-to-apply-for-wazir-e-azam-apna-ghar-program-e2-80-93-ghar-ho-tu-apna-step-by-step-application-guidejpg.png\",\"faqs\":\"[{\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can I apply if I already own a house?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"No. The scheme is only for first-time homeowners with no housing unit in their name.\\\"},{\\\"question\\\":\\\"Do I have to apply online?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Not necessarily. You can use the portal or go through a participating bank\'s branch.\\\"},{\\\"question\\\":\\\"Is there a processing fee?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"No. There\'s also no early repayment penalty.\\\"},{\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can freelancers apply?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Yes, through the informal income category. Expect to provide stronger documentation.\\\"},{\\\"question\\\":\\\"What happens after 10 years?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The 5% rate ends and a market-linked rate applies, so installments may rise.\\\"}]\"}', 'https://fsadvisory.pk/admin/blogs/10', '203.101.188.87', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/157.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', NULL, '2026-11-16 11:35:56', '2026-11-16 11:35:56'),
(1192, 'App\\Models\\User', 2, 'updated', 'App\\Models\\Blog', 10, '{\"meta_title\":null,\"meta_description\":null}', '{\"meta_title\":\"Wazir-e-Azam Apna Ghar Programme: How to Apply\",\"meta_description\":\"Learn how to apply for the Wazir-e-Azam Apna Ghar Programme: eligibility, documents, 5% markup loans up to Rs10 million and a step-by-step portal guide.\"}', 'https://fsadvisory.pk/admin/blogs/10', '203.101.188.87', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/157.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', NULL, '2026-11-16 11:36:45', '2026-11-16 11:36:45'),
(1193, 'App\\Models\\User', 2, 'updated', 'App\\Models\\Page', 177, '{\"is_published\":1,\"meta_title\":\"Grace Tower | Luxury Properties\",\"meta_description\":\"Explore Grace Tower. Discover luxury residences, pricing, master plan, and world-class amenities.\",\"meta_keywords\":\"Grace Tower, luxury villas, properties\"}', '{\"is_published\":false,\"meta_title\":\"Grace Tower Naya Nazimabad: Apartments & Shops Karachi\",\"meta_description\":\"Grace Tower in Naya Nazimabad\\u2019s Business Enclave offers apartments and ground-floor shops. See project details, location and how to enquire.\",\"meta_keywords\":\"Grace Tower Naya Nazimabad\"}', 'https://fsadvisory.pk/admin/projects/69', '203.101.188.87', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/156.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', NULL, '2026-11-16 11:38:33', '2026-11-16 11:38:33'),
(1194, 'App\\Models\\User', 2, 'updated', 'App\\Models\\PageSection', 1422, '{\"content\":\"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Grace Tower\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"badge\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"bg_image\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"bg_image_alt\\\":\\\"\\\"}\"}', '{\"content\":\"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Grace Tower at Business Enclave, Naya Nazimabad Karachi\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":null,\\\"badge\\\":null,\\\"bg_image\\\":null,\\\"bg_image_alt\\\":\\\"Grace Tower at Business Enclave, Naya Nazimabad Karachi\\\",\\\"image_alt\\\":\\\"Grace Tower at Business Enclave, Naya Nazimabad Karachi\\\"}\"}', 'https://fsadvisory.pk/admin/projects/69', '203.101.188.87', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/156.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', NULL, '2026-11-16 11:38:33', '2026-11-16 11:38:33'),
(1195, 'App\\Models\\User', 2, 'updated', 'App\\Models\\PageSection', 1424, '{\"content\":\"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"video_poster\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"video_src\\\":\\\"\\\"}\"}', '{\"content\":\"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Grace Tower by Naya Nazimabad\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"<div>Grace Tower is a mixed-use project inside Naya Nazimabad, Karachi. The official project page describes elegantly designed apartments together with premium retail shops on the ground floor, in the heart of the Business Enclave. The building rises up to four floors. Unit sizes, price, payment plan, approvals and possession have not been published on that page, so buyers should confirm them directly with the developer\\\\u2019s sales team.<\\\\\\/div>\\\",\\\"video_poster\\\":null,\\\"video_src\\\":\\\"\\\"}\"}', 'https://fsadvisory.pk/admin/projects/69', '203.101.188.87', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/156.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', NULL, '2026-11-16 11:38:33', '2026-11-16 11:38:33'),
(1196, 'App\\Models\\User', 2, 'updated', 'App\\Models\\PageSection', 1425, '{\"content\":\"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"items\\\":[]}\"}', '{\"content\":\"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Grace Tower Amenities\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"No amenity schedule has been published for Grace Tower on the official page. The page lists modern architecture, a prime business-centre location and world-class fixtures as the project\\\\u2019s main features. Naya Nazimabad\\\\u2019s community facilities, such as the Gymkhana and Jama Masjid, are listed separately on the community\\\\u2019s website and should not be treated as Grace Tower amenities unless the developer confirms it.\\\",\\\"items\\\":[]}\"}', 'https://fsadvisory.pk/admin/projects/69', '203.101.188.87', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/156.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', NULL, '2026-11-16 11:38:33', '2026-11-16 11:38:33'),
