(1221, 'App\\Models\\User', 2, 'updated', 'App\\Models\\PageSection', 1410, '{\"content\":\"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Peace Apartments at Naya Nazimabad Karachi\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":null,\\\"badge\\\":null,\\\"bg_image\\\":\\\"\\\\\\/uploads\\\\\\/pages\\\\\\/1794827760_6afae5f03980b.jpg\\\",\\\"bg_image_alt\\\":\\\"Peace Apartments at Naya Nazimabad Karachi\\\",\\\"image_alt\\\":\\\"Peace Apartments at Naya Nazimabad Karachi\\\"}\"}', '{\"content\":\"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Peace Apartments Naya Nazimabad: Price & 1% Payment Plan\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":null,\\\"badge\\\":null,\\\"bg_image\\\":\\\"\\\\\\/uploads\\\\\\/pages\\\\\\/1794827760_6afae5f03980b.jpg\\\",\\\"bg_image_alt\\\":\\\"Peace Apartments Naya Nazimabad: Price & 1% Payment Plan\\\",\\\"image_alt\\\":\\\"Peace Apartments Naya Nazimabad: Price & 1% Payment Plan\\\"}\"}', 'https://fsadvisory.pk/admin/projects/68', '203.101.188.87', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/157.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', NULL, '2026-11-16 11:42:32', '2026-11-16 11:42:32'),
(1222, 'App\\Models\\User', 2, 'created', 'App\\Models\\Blog', 11, '[]', '{\"title\":\"Why Invest in Dubai Real Estate from Pakistan in 2027\",\"slug\":\"why-invest-in-dubai-real-estate-from-pakistan-in-2027\",\"category\":\"Real Estate\",\"short_content\":\"Picture a family in Lahore that has watched its rupee savings lose ground against the dollar for years.\",\"content\":\"<p>Picture a family in Lahore that has watched its rupee savings lose ground against the dollar for years. Now picture that same family looking at an apartment priced in dirhams, a currency pegged to the dollar. That contrast is a big part of why more people want to invest in Dubai real estate from Pakistan, and why it has stopped being a rich person\'s hobby.<\\/p><h2>Why So Many Pakistanis Look At Dubai<\\/h2><p>Pakistan ranked second among foreign buyers of Dubai property in 2023 and sat fourth by 2025. One report this year counts around 17,000 Pakistanis owning roughly 23,000 properties there, worth more than $13 billion.<\\/p><p>The pull is very easy to explain:<\\/p><ul><li>The rupee keeps weakening<\\/li><li>Rental yields of six to ten percent a year are often quoted for decent areas.<\\/li><li>The UAE charges no income tax on rent, and no capital gains tax on residential property for individual investors.<\\/li><li>Direct flights and a large Pakistani community make the city feel familiar.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>One more perk worth knowing is that property bought at AED 2 million or more qualifies for the 10-year Golden Visa. Dubai property for overseas investors often includes extras like that, but don\'t stretch your budget to hit a number.<\\/p><p>That\'s the case for Dubai property investment for Pakistanis, and it\'s a fair one. It just isn\'t the whole story, which is why interest to invest in Dubai real estate from Pakistan keeps growing alongside the warnings.<\\/p><h2>Can You Invest In Dubai Real Estate From Pakistan Without Moving?<\\/h2><p>Yes. Foreigners can buy freehold property in designated areas with full ownership, and residency isn\'t required. The Dubai Land Department handles registration and title transfer. The main government cost is a 4 percent transfer fee plus a small admin charge. UAE banks do lend to Pakistani nationals, but terms vary and residents generally get better options.<\\/p><p>So if you want to buy property in Dubai from Pakistan, nothing stops you. Use a licensed local agent instead of a social media ad, confirm the developer\'s track record, and check that the project is registered with the regulator.<\\/p><h2>Off-plan Vs Ready Properties<\\/h2><p>Plenty of people who invest in Dubai real estate from Pakistan start with a staged payment plan.<\\/p><p>Off-plan properties in Dubai usually want 10 to 20 percent up front, with the rest spread over construction milestones across 18 to 36 months. Buyers\' money sits in regulated escrow, which lowers completion risk but doesn\'t erase it.<\\/p><p>Ready units cost more at the start, yet you can see the actual flat and estimate real rent. If you can\'t comfortably wait two or three years, an easy payment plan shouldn\'t talk you into off-plan properties in Dubai.<\\/p><table><tbody><tr><th>Factor<\\/th><th>Off-Plan<\\/th><th>Ready Property<\\/th><\\/tr><tr><td>Down Payment<\\/td><td>10\\u201320% upfront<\\/td><td>Higher upfront cost<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Payment Plan<\\/td><td>Staged instalments<\\/td><td>Mostly upfront<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Timeline<\\/td><td>18\\u201336 months<\\/td><td>Immediate possession<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Rental Income<\\/td><td>After handover<\\/td><td>Can start immediately<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Best For<\\/td><td>Long-term investors<\\/td><td>Immediate rental returns or personal use<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><h2>Where The Money Tends To Go<\\/h2><p>Pakistani buyers keep returning to a handful of communities.<\\/p><h3>Dubai Marina<\\/h3><p>Strong for short-term rentals, with one-bedrooms starting around AED 900,000 to 1,200,000.<\\/p><h3>Business Bay<\\/h3><p>Popular with corporate tenants, priced much like Marina.<\\/p><h3>Jumeirah Village Circle<\\/h3><p>The cheaper entry point, roughly AED 600,000 to 900,000, often with a higher percentage yield.<\\/p><h3>Arabian Ranches<\\/h3><p>A family villa and townhouse community, with rental returns above six percent.<\\/p><h3>Tilal Al Ghaf<\\/h3><p>Another family favourite, also with returns above six percent.<\\/p><p>Area matters more than people think. A weak building can underperform even in a strong market.<\\/p><h2>The Costs Nobody Puts in the Brochure<\\/h2><p>Service charges and maintenance chip away at your rent. Vacancy happens. Anyone planning to invest in Dubai real estate from Pakistan should start with a budget in dirhams after all costs, not the headline price. Talk to your bank and a tax adviser too, about moving money out of Pakistan and declaring the asset properly.<\\/p><p>The practical worry is who looks after the place. Property managers handle tenants, pricing, cleaning and repairs, and you have to review a monthly report.<\\/p><h2>Looking Ahead<\\/h2><p>Earlier this year, tension in the Gulf made some Pakistani buyers pause, and interest picked up once things calmed. Keep that in mind for Dubai real estate 2027. The market is regulated, yet Dubai property for overseas investors still carries the usual risks like oversupply, weak tenant demand, and buying on hype. Before you invest in Dubai real estate from Pakistan, check the latest regional news, and size any Dubai real estate 2027 purchase around cash flow you can actually hold.<\\/p><p>The smartest move if you want to invest in Dubai real estate from Pakistan is also the least exciting one. Pick the asset that fits your budget, timeline and income goals. Skip the loudest launch. Done well, Dubai property investment for Pakistanis is a slow, structured plan, not a gamble.<\\/p>\",\"cover_image\":\"\\/images\\/blogs\\/1794829488_cover_rove-home-apartments-at-downtown-dubai2.webp\",\"faqs\":\"[{\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can I invest in Dubai real estate from Pakistan without visiting?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Yes. Freehold purchase doesn\'t need residency, and agents and managers can handle most steps remotely.\\\"},{\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can I buy property in Dubai from Pakistan on a small budget?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Possibly. Off-plan asks 10 to 20 percent up front, and areas like JVC cost less than Marina.\\\"},{\\\"question\\\":\\\"Is rental income taxed in Dubai?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The UAE charges no income tax on rent. Check your Pakistani tax obligations separately.\\\"},{\\\"question\\\":\\\"Is off-plan safer than ready property?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Neither is automatically safer. Escrow protects payments, but delivery and developer quality still matter.\\\"},{\\\"question\\\":\\\"Is it still safe to invest in Dubai real estate from Pakistan?\\\",\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Many see Dubai as one of the region\'s steadier markets, but regional tension can slow deals. Do your homework first.\\\"}]\",\"status\":\"draft\",\"is_published\":false,\"author\":\"Saima Editorial\",\"meta_title\":null,\"meta_description\":null,\"meta_keywords\":null,\"id\":11}', 'https://fsadvisory.pk/admin/blogs', '203.101.188.87', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/157.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', NULL, '2026-11-16 11:44:48', '2026-11-16 11:44:48'),
